cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "Please cite the article (reference to be added on publication) and this repository."
type: software
title: "5-rad: CT radiomics of the future pancreatic remnant and CR-POPF after distal pancreatectomy"
abstract: >-
  Code, de-identified data and results of the single-center study "Preoperative Prediction of Postoperative Pancreatic
  Fistula After Distal Pancreatectomy Using a Sparse Radiomic Signature of the Pancreatic Remnant" (Beaujon Hospital,
  AP-HP, Clichy, France). In 251 patients who underwent distal pancreatectomy in 2019-2025 (50 clinically relevant
  postoperative pancreatic fistulas, ISGPS grade B or C), radiomic features of the future pancreatic remnant
  (head-isthmus region) on preoperative portal venous CT were harmonized with ComBat, prefiltered without the outcome and
  selected with Stabl; an elastic-net logistic regression on five features (5-rad) was validated internally by bootstrap
  .632+ and strict nested cross-validation, compared with the D-FRS and DISPAIR-FRS, and used to define rule-out and
  rule-in risk groups. run_all.sh, or the Docker image, regenerates Tables 1-2, Supplementary Tables 1 and 4, Figures 1
  and 3-5 and Supplementary Figures 1-3 from the de-identified radiomic-feature and clinical tables in data/. CT images and
  segmentation masks are not included.
license: MIT
keywords:
  - radiomics
  - computed tomography
  - distal pancreatectomy
  - postoperative pancreatic fistula
  - CR-POPF
  - prediction model
  - stability selection
  - Stabl
  - elastic net
  - ComBat harmonization
  - PyRadiomics
  - internal validation
